## Description of the bug

numba leaks one small allocation per raising call when a jitted function writes
into an array argument after (in code order) a nested njit call
that raises.  The write doesn't have to actually execute, its presence in
the body is enough.

My guess is the leaked block
holds a reference to the array argument and when the
caller passes a freshly allocated array each call, the array is
pinned too and RSS grows without bound (second demo).

Remove the write loop (or inline the raise into the caller) and
the leak disappears.

Seen with numba 0.66.0, numpy 2.4.6, python 3.14.6 (linux).

