#### Bug Report Checklist

- [x] Have you provided a full/minimal spec to reproduce the issue?
- [x] Have you validated the input using an OpenAPI validator?
- [x] Have you [tested with the latest master](https://github.com/OpenAPITools/openapi-generator/wiki/FAQ#how-to-test-with-the-latest-master-of-openapi-generator) to confirm the issue still exists?
- [x] Have you searched for related issues/PRs?
- [x] What's the actual output vs expected output?
- [ ] [Optional] Sponsorship to speed up the bug fix or feature request ([example](https://github.com/OpenAPITools/openapi-generator/issues/6178))

##### Description

When generating typescript-angular code, it was noticed that a field in a schema got the description of a seemingly unrelated query parameter. The field is an optional, nullable string. Changing the type in any way (making it required, making it non-nullable) leads to the correct description being assigned.

Generating code for other languages had the same issue, so it sounds like it's some problem prior to actual code generation.

##### openapi-generator version

Tried v7.23.0, v7.24.0, v7.25.0.

##### OpenAPI declaration file content or url

```json
{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "minimal example - description bug",
    "description": "-",
    "version": "0.0.0"
  },
  "paths": {
    "/book": {
      "get": {
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Book"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/book-with-pages": {
      "get": {
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "conflicting-param",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "anyOf": [
                {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ],
              "description": "WRONG DESCRIPTION! (schema)"
            },
            "description": "WRONG DESCRIPTION! (parameter)"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Book"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "schemas": {
      "Book": {
        "properties": {
          "broken_field": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "description": "Correct description."
          }
        },
        "title": "Book",
        "type": "object"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

##### Generation Details

No specific configuration:

```shell
docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/local" openapitools/openapi-generator-cli:v7.25.0 generate -i /local/openapi-spec-minimal.json -g typescript-angular -o /local/clientsdk
```

Generates in `book.ts`:

```typescript
export interface Book { 
    /**
     * WRONG DESCRIPTION! (schema)
     */
    broken_field?: string | null;
}
```

Expected output:

```typescript
export interface Book { 
    /**
     * Correct description.
     */
    broken_field?: string | null;
}
```

##### Related issues/PRs

I could not find any, but it might be hard to find just based on the description.

