**Affects PMD Version:** 7.28.0 (also 7.29.0-SNAPSHOT)

**Description:**

For an `ExecutorService pool`, javac compiles `pool.submit(() -> { while (true) { } })` to `submit(Callable)` and PMD resolves it to `submit(Runnable)`. For `pool.submit(() -> { if (flag) { throw new IllegalStateException(); } })` it is the other way round. javac selects `submit(Runnable)`, PMD `submit(Callable)`.

`LambdaMirrorImpl.isLambdaBodyCompatible` treats a block body without `return expr;` as value-compatible when the block contains a `throw` statement:

https://github.com/pmd/pmd/blob/5c9271c586d69d4386f14a2f997f9d4ff56a0a75/pmd-java/src/main/java/net/sourceforge/pmd/lang/java/types/internal/infer/ast/LambdaMirrorImpl.java#L141-L148

JLS 15.27.2 asks instead whether the block can complete normally (JLS 14.22). The body `{ while (true) { } }` cannot complete normally and is value-compatible. The second body can complete normally and is not. Line 144 has the comment `// normally we should be determining whether the block must complete abruptly on all paths`. `AbruptCompletionAnalysis.canCompleteNormally` in `symbols/table/internal` implements JLS 14.22. It is package-private, and it recognizes a constant true loop condition only as the literal `true` (line 249), so a body such as `{ while (1 < 2) { } }` needs the constant expression rule of JLS 14.22 as well.

Found while working on #7136.

**Code Sample demonstrating the issue:**

```java
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;

public class Submit {
    void t(ExecutorService pool, boolean flag) {
        pool.submit(() -> { while (true) { } });
        pool.submit(() -> { if (flag) { throw new IllegalStateException(); } });
    }
}
```

**Steps to reproduce:**

1. `javac Submit.java`, also with `--release 8`, then `javap -c -p Submit`. `Submit.t` calls `submit:(Ljava/util/concurrent/Callable;)` on line 5 and `submit:(Ljava/lang/Runnable;)` on line 6.
2. Run PMD on the file with the XPath rule `//MethodCall[pmd-java:matchesSig("java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService#submit(java.lang.Runnable)")]`. It reports line 5 and not line 6.

**Running PMD through:** *Other* (PmdAnalysis API)

