**Affects PMD Version:** 7.24.0

**Rule:** UselessPureMethodCall — https://docs.pmd-code.org/latest/pmd_rules_java_errorprone.html#uselesspuremethodcall

**Description:**

`UselessPureMethodCall` correctly flags `Stream#anyMatch` / `findAny` / `count` calls whose return value is ignored, but does not fire when the very same pattern is written against the primitive specialisations `IntStream`, `LongStream`, or `DoubleStream`. Those primitive specialisations expose exactly the same terminal operations with the same purity properties, so the violation should be reported uniformly.

**Code Sample demonstrating the issue:**

```java
import java.util.stream.IntStream;
import java.util.stream.LongStream;
import java.util.stream.DoubleStream;
import java.util.stream.Stream;

public class StreamReproducer {

    // Flagged correctly (UselessPureMethodCall on anyMatch):
